===============================================================================
SHIPPED INSIDE Utter.app
===============================================================================

These are placed in the application bundle by scripts/build-app.sh and are
present in every installed copy and every DMG.


1. whisper.cpp - version 1.9.2
   https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp
   Licence: MIT
   Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors

   Consumed as the prebuilt macOS xcframework
   `whisper-v1.9.2-xcframework.zip`, declared as a `binaryTarget` and pinned by
   SHA-256 checksum in Package.swift. scripts/build-app.sh copies
   `whisper.framework` out of the resolved artefact into
   `Utter.app/Contents/Frameworks/`.

   The upstream release archive contains no licence file of its own, so nothing
   supplies this notice implicitly. MIT requires the copyright notice and
   permission notice in "all copies or substantial portions of the Software";
   shipping the framework inside the app is such a copy. This file is how that
   obligation is met.


2. Whisper speech recognition model weights
   https://github.com/openai/whisper
   Licence: MIT
   Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI

   `ggml-small.en-q5_1.bin` is bundled at
   `Utter.app/Contents/Resources/Models/` so that transcription works offline on
   first launch with no download step. The larger tiers Utter offers in
   Settings are the same weights at a different size; they are downloaded by the
   user on request and are not part of the bundle.


3. ggml / GGUF conversions of the Whisper weights
   https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
   Repository licence tag: mit

   The bundled `.bin` file is not OpenAI's original checkpoint. It is a
   quantized ggml conversion of it, and the conversion published in the
   repository above is the one Utter ships and the one it downloads from. The
   credit is owed to that conversion work as well as to the original weights.


