USED ONLY TO BUILD OR TEST UTTER - NOT REDISTRIBUTED
===============================================================================

Nothing in this section is copied into Utter.app. These are developer
dependencies, and an installed copy of Utter contains no part of them.


4. Swift Testing - version 0.99.0
   https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-testing
   Licence: Apache License 2.0 with the Runtime Library Exception
   Copyright (c) 2023 Apple Inc. and the Swift project authors

   TEST-ONLY. It is a dependency of the `UtterKitTests` target and of nothing
   else, so it is linked into the test binary and never into the app. See
   Package.swift, where it appears only under `.testTarget`. It is declared as a
   package dependency rather than taken from the toolchain because a
   Command-Line-Tools-only machine ships neither XCTest nor a built-in Testing
   module.

   Its Runtime Library Exception reads:

     As an exception, if you use this Software to compile your source code and
     portions of this Software are embedded into the binary product as a result,
     you may redistribute such product without providing attribution as would
     otherwise be required by Sections 4(a), 4(b) and 4(d) of the License.

   The exception is noted for completeness rather than relied on: no part of
   Swift Testing is embedded in Utter.app in the first place.

   The full Apache License 2.0 text is in this repository's LICENSE file, which
   is the same licence Utter itself uses.


5. Pillow
   https://python-pillow.github.io/
   Licence: MIT-CMU

   BUILD-TIME ONLY. Pillow is imported by the asset-generation scripts under
   scripts/ and tools/mochi/ - the app icon, the menu-bar template image, the
   DMG installer background, and the companion sprite packs. Those scripts run
   on the build machine and write PNG files; the PNGs are shipped, Pillow is
   not. See requirements.txt.

   Utter contains no Python. A machine that only wants to run the app never
   installs Pillow, and a machine building from source needs it only when the
   generated art is missing or out of date.
